\par This Customs Response Message (CUSRES) permits the transfer of data from a customs administration:
\par - to acknowledge the receipt of the message - to indicate whether the information received is correct or if there are errors (i.e.  accepted without errors, accepted with errors, rejected, etc.) - to inform the sender of the status of the customs declarat
i
on (i.e.  goods released, goods for examination, documents required, etc.) - to transmit additional information as agreed between parties (i.e.  tax information, quantity information, etc.) - to respond to batched messages (i.e.  CUSDEC, CUSCAR, CUSREP, C
USEXP).
\par Note: this message is not meant to replace the functionality of the CONTRL message.
